From 37f9a874e76f3879085563d38ee2a36e0bdd4dbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 18:59:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XD Netplay: deterministic XD clock keeps the recompilers in
 mixed-architecture rooms (v1.5.11)

v1.5.10 put mixed rooms on the Cached Interpreter, which is correct but far
too slow to play. XD reads time through exactly two functions; two
recompilers split blocks differently so those reads differed by a few
dozen cycles between machines, and XD builds its GBA link key and battle
RNG seed from them.

- HLE Replace hooks on OSGetTick (0x800b225c) and OSGetTime (0x800b2244)
  for GXXE01, installed from PatchFixedFunctions when the netplay-synced
  session flag is on: value = synced TB start + salt + 675675 * XD's own
  frame counter (0x804EA8A8) + a per-call step for spin-waits; frame-exact
  for the stamps that feed game state, real time base for alarms, audio,
  save timestamps, reset and crash paths; host-synced RNG seed and link
  key; per-site ordinals for the CARD LCG seeds.
- Host policy: mixed room + XD -> clock on, recompilers kept, random salt
  and seed per session, apploader boot forced, accurate NaNs pinned, chat
  notice. ForceCommonCoreOnMixedArch is now the opt-in 'safest' mode.
- Wire: three NetSettings fields appended after the SRAM bytes; guest
  fallback uses its own recompiler when the clock is on.
- Time-base desync detector tolerates the recompiler skew when the clock
  is on.
- Logs: cpu line xd_clock/xd_salt/xd_seed/xd_period/xd_inc, xd lines lf/lt,
  xdclk lines on link events.
